### THIS IS OPTIONAL!!! Tailscale integration

Infrastructure-as-code tools like Pulumi or Terraform make it easy to spin up new resources like servers, or containers for your tailnet. Pre-authentication keys (“auth keys” for short) allow you to register them as they are being provisioned without needing to sign in via a web browser.

Auth keys can be either one-off, useful when you can’t authenticate a device directly; or reusable, for multiple uses or when connecting multiple nodes. Auth keys authenticate a machine using the identity of the person who generated the key.

Generating a key:
Open the Keys page of the admin console. Choose what kind of key you’d like to generate. Also choose the number of days, between 1 and 90 inclusive, for the key expiry. The default is 90 days.

Generate an auth key that has ACL tags, so that when used, the device’s identity is the tag. You can also generate an auth key that is pre-authorized so it will be automatically approved if you have device approval enabled for your network. 

